      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-04T00:29:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t get it. The free_blocks_ data structire is a std::set allocated with the default allocator. How can an madvise on the large object space affect memory allocated with the default, presumably scudo, allocator? The free_blocks_ data structure should be completely separate from the blocks managed by FreeListSpace.",
