      "writtenOn": "2024-12-27T00:25:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAICT, you\u0027re assuming for performance reasons that ptrs is address ordered? If so, please document that here, as in \"Deallocate all num_ptrs objects referenced by ptrs. Performance is much better if ptrs is address-ordered.\"\n\nAlso please add enough documentation to the caller(s) to make it plausible to the reader that the list is in fact address-ordered.\n\nAlso please check and document here that Free() and FreeList() are only ever called during a GC, and thus can never be called concurrently. Your changes rely on that to avoid races in the data structure access. Unfortunately, there are no GUARDED_BY annotations to check any of this.",
